# Lab R640 disks (2026-09-26)

Before SSH, `racadm`, flash, or any MegaRAID idea, read [`docs/runbooks/r640_perc_lab.md`](docs/runbooks/r640_perc_lab.md). That file is the map. [`docs/m8_state.md`](docs/m8_state.md) is the persist history.

Ubuntu 26.04 is the standing OS. RayNu is not booted. Service tag **D0324Y2**. iDRAC `https://10.99.99.24` (3.34.34.34). SSH `vikkp@10.99.99.151` (DHCP; prompt `raynusrv1`). Host key `SHA256:e8RgOlR34L9cvcIbhNRn12T1AVof8MiqlzmsZm6az1I`.

Disk letters move. Match size:

| Size | Name | Rule |
|------|------|------|
| ~400 GB | **UBUNTU0**, boot | Ubuntu `/` and `/boot/efi`. Do not shrink, delete, or format. |
| ~2.9 TB | **RAYNU-SPARE** | Empty. Do not partition, mkfs, mount, or LVM. |
| ~3.8 GB | Cruzer, label `RAYNUV` | Flash target. Never pick a disk by `/dev/sdX`. |
| ~298 GB | Toshiba | Alpine persist. Do not format. Do not flash. 8 GiB virtio cap stays. |

Open only the **PERC H740P Mini** (integrated, serial `97101GC`, `0000:18:00.0`). Do not open the **H840** in slot 1. Do not Clear Configuration again.

The empty spare is a prerequisite. It is not `RAYNU-V-M8-PERC-LUN-OK`. `piece_perc_pct` stays 15 until a mailbox read of the spare lives on iron. Host/CI never print that marker. A5 (`auth.token`) is parked.

**M8.7** is the Fusion mailbox milestone (`docs/m8_plan.md`). Iron `22ce3728` read H740P Mini scratch pad 0 as `0xb73c0fed` (READY, max commands 4077, queues 128, RDPQ, `mapped=1`) at `18:00.0`. The H840 (`3b:00.0` `1028:1fc9`) stayed unmapped. `outbound_msg_0` was 0. That is the xscale register, not a reset. The low 16 bits of scratch pad 0 are max commands, not a reset request. The next EFI posts one IOC init and one LD list to port `0xC0` because the nibble is already READY. It does not store the doorbell. `skip PERC` stays. F11 is a one-shot of the Cruzer (label `RAYNUV`) after Ubuntu is the OS. Do not F11 `22ce3728`, `2dd2b412`, or `cc03d01b` again. Do not reset the adapter. `mapped=0` or a state nibble other than READY stops the milestone. A nonzero `perc ioc status` stops it too.

iDRAC 3.34 cannot delete virtual disks from the web UI (RAC0503). F2 → Device Settings → H740P Mini is the configuration path. Do not repeat it.
